\documentclass{article}
\title{Language Models for Automated Theorem Proving}
\author{E. Ruder}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Introduction}
Recent work proves that language models can discover non-trivial mathematical proofs. Our system always finds a proof when one exists within the search depth. It is the best prover on the miniF2F benchmark. The model never hallucinates invalid steps because every step is checked by the kernel. Our approach guarantees complete automation of undergraduate-level exercises.
\section{Evaluation}
We evaluate on miniF2F and ProofNet.
\end{document}
